{
  "texts": [
    {
      "content": "The Azurleaf Bulb is notable for its large bluish leaf with prominent venation, ",
      "left": "716px",
      "top": "237.3px",
      "scale": "2.200000000000001",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "15px",
      "color": "rgb(3, 3, 3)"
    },
    {
      "content": "Its root system is short and fibrous, allowing it to anchor itself in unstable or viscous soils.",
      "left": "705.3px",
      "top": "333.1px",
      "scale": "2.200000000000001",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "15px",
      "color": "rgb(3, 3, 3)"
    },
    {
      "content": "Within Maxkodia’s forests, this plant functions as a bioindicator of iron-rich grounds,\n\n",
      "left": "725.8px",
      "top": "380px",
      "scale": "2.200000000000001",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "15px",
      "color": "rgb(3, 3, 3)"
    },
    {
      "content": "concentrating metallic traces in its foliar tissues.",
      "left": "773px",
      "top": "430.1px",
      "scale": "2.200000000000001",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "15px",
      "color": "rgb(3, 3, 3)"
    },
    {
      "content": "supported by a fleshy orange basal bulb.",
      "left": "784.5px",
      "top": "281.5px",
      "scale": "2.200000000000001",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "15px",
      "color": "rgb(3, 3, 3)"
    },
    {
      "content": "At night, its leaves reflect the binary starlight with a faint glow,",
      "left": "752px",
      "top": "474.6px",
      "scale": "2.200000000000001",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "15px",
      "color": "rgb(3, 3, 3)"
    },
    {
      "content": "serving as a landmark for small luminescent insects.",
